      "writtenOn": "2022-11-22T18:20:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see value in decoupling the encoding and decoding into separate coverage flows.\n\nOne example case where it make difference is when the first fuzz call, for example fuzz_encode, crashes. If we call fuzz_encode and fuzz_decode successively on the same data, this would not let fuzzer to call fuzz_decode, and this may prevent fuzzer from discovering some new branch in decoding.\n\nWhereas selecting either encode or decode lets fuzzer explore coverage for encode and decode independently of each other.",
      "parentUuid": "471aded2_c6b3d126",
